# ExaBGP qa/old/5.0/qa/encoding/api-multisession (ExaBGP 685f772e4e): .ci and .msg joined, options spelt option=
option=allowed:the recording comes from a session with BGP multi-session, which ze does not support (draft-ietf-idr-bgp-multisession is not an RFC): the 5.0 helper's family-allowed ipv4-unicast route 1.2.0.0/24 names a session ze never has, so ze drops it and sends the family-allowed in-open route 9.9.9.0/24 instead, as ExaBGP does for a neighbor without the capability (docs/exabgp/exabgp-differences.md)
